{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43279 - PROTEIN:5942",
  "verbalization": "Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- is implicated in the target relationship with Tankyrase-2 through a multi-step pathway involving the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14. This entity is a common target of multiple compounds, including 5-Oxobrucine and 24-Methylenecycloartanone, which in turn direct their activity toward Tankyrase-2. The evidence suggests that Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- may act as a modulator of Tankyrase-2 through the regulation of the proteasome, which is a key player in cellular protein degradation and has been shown to interact with Tankyrase-2 in various biological contexts. The presence of multiple compounds with similar target profiles further supports the idea that Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- may function as a scaffold or regulatory agent that influences Tankyrase-2 activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential role of the proteasome in mediating the effects of Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3alpha)- on Tankyrase-2, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
